    "long_instructions": "#####Consider the JSON array below:\r\n\r\n```\r\nconst items = [\r\n  {\r\n    name: \"Notebook\",\r\n    price: 3.99,\r\n    category: \"school\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    name: \"Water Bottle\",\r\n    price: 12.5,\r\n    category: \"supplies\"\r\n  }\r\n];\r\n```\r\n> 1. Write the dot-notation path to access the price of the first item.\r\n> \r\n> 2. Explain how you would use .map() to create a new array that only includes the name and price from each item.\r\n\r\n#####You do not need to write perfect code for Question 2. You may explain your answer in plain language or pseudocode.",
